From 030c284fb7e3425ced0001b1fa47d79739a2f4e2 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: x <x@y.z>
Date: Sat, 24 Oct 2026 23:27:07 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 07/21] irq: carry IRQ numbers wider than u8 through the irq
 scheme

DT irqchips hand out virqs up to 1024, but irq_trigger, the irq scheme
handles and the dtb reservation helpers took a u8. trigger_virq truncated
the virq with `as u8`, open_phandle_irq rejected any virq above 223, and the
aarch64/riscv64 console handlers unwrapped a u8 conversion, so a GICv3 SPI
such as SDM845 GENI uart9 (SPI 354, virq 386) would panic on delivery.

Use u16 for scheme IRQ numbers (x86 vectors stay u8), size the DT queue
table from the irqchip descriptor count, drop out-of-range triggers instead
of indexing past the table, keep full phandles in phandle handles, and stop
irq_iter_for from truncating hwirqs.

Co-Authored-By: Cursor <noreply@cursor.com>
Co-Authored-By: Codex <noreply@openai.com>
